From 099019c6c68f55939a89f09f76c184253df97728 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dimitri Geelen <dimitri@geelenandcompany.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 14:17:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] note resolve: an already-fixed observation can leave
 the inbox, with a carrier (from 832 T-914/T-1028)

The inbox's largest class is "already fixed, the content lives elsewhere". Dismiss records a
decision nobody made; promote files a duplicate task. With no resolve verb those stay pending
forever, so the inbox grows monotonically.
`fw note resolve OBS-NNN --carrier <T-id | path> [--reason "..."]` sets status resolved and
records resolved_carrier, resolved_carrier_kind (task|path), resolved_at and resolved_reason.
The carrier is MANDATORY and VALIDATED (a T-id must have a task file; a path must exist):
resolved-with-no-pointer is the same defect the promote fix removes. Refusals write nothing;
only pending observations resolve; every other inbox entry stays byte-identical.
Applies on top of the promote commit.
Probe: tests/unit/test_t1021_note_resolve.sh (hermetic scratch project, real CLI).
Before: 5/7 (the four refusal legs pass only because the verb is absent). After: 7/7.
Unchanged by this and the promote commit together: 19 suites that touch observe.sh, fw note or
inbox.yaml (fw_note.bats, lib_promote.bats, note_capture_guard.bats, note_exit_status.bats, ...).
